773
01:25:35,636 --> 01:25:38,756
Netflix is revolutionizing the way we watch TV.

774
01:25:38,756 --> 01:25:43,136
But some fear that Netflix could be closing the curtains on the big screen.

775
01:25:43,916 --> 01:25:49,796
So, is there any evidence to suggest that our love for streaming movies at home could spell the end for cinema?

776
01:25:50,855 --> 01:25:55,176
US-based company Netflix has had more than a few reasons to celebrate this year.

777
01:25:55,855 --> 01:26:00,916
It's added a record-breaking number of paid users to its online streaming service in 2018.

778
01:26:01,596 --> 01:26:04,556
Now topping 139 million worldwide.

779
01:26:04,695 --> 01:26:08,115
That's three times the number of accounts just five years ago.

780
01:26:08,115 --> 01:26:11,536
Keep in mind that more than one person could be using an account.

781
01:26:11,956 --> 01:26:13,636
So, its reach is even bigger.

782
01:26:14,476 --> 01:26:17,096
The USA is Netflix's top market globally.

783
01:26:17,536 --> 01:26:20,536
With over 40% of all paid users based there.

784
01:26:20,836 --> 01:26:24,775
The company has also invested heavily into producing original content.

785
01:26:25,296 --> 01:26:27,235
Including big movie blockbusters.

786
01:26:27,855 --> 01:26:34,235
Analysts estimate that the company spent $13 billion on titles like Narcos and Bird Box in 2018.

787
01:26:34,235 --> 01:26:40,996
That would be enough to make Titanic one of the most expensive films ever made 65 times.

788
01:26:41,336 --> 01:26:43,136
Its efforts seem to be paying off.

789
01:26:43,655 --> 01:26:47,516
This year, its critically acclaimed film Roma has earned a streaming service.

790
01:26:47,756 --> 01:26:50,176
Its first Best Picture Oscar nomination.

791
01:26:50,576 --> 01:26:51,976
With 10 in total.

792
01:26:51,976 --> 01:26:55,456
You might think that can only benefit the box office.

793
01:26:55,456 --> 01:27:01,556
But Netflix has been criticised for showing films in a relatively small number of movie theatres.

794
01:27:01,996 --> 01:27:03,456
And for a limited time.

795
01:27:03,695 --> 01:27:05,876
Before streaming them on its own site.

796
01:27:06,536 --> 01:27:09,536
So, are there any signs that cinemas are suffering?

797
01:27:10,195 --> 01:27:11,076
Not really.

798
01:27:11,076 --> 01:27:15,536
While analysts said that 2017 was a tough year for movie makers.

799
01:27:15,936 --> 01:27:18,256
Last year saw a boost for the box office.

800
01:27:18,836 --> 01:27:22,516
Worldwide, cinemas made over $41.5 billion.

801
01:27:23,235 --> 01:27:26,136
That's 2.6% more than in 2017.

802
01:27:26,756 --> 01:27:27,916
The top three markets.

803
01:27:28,136 --> 01:27:30,115
The USA, China and the UK.

804
01:27:30,676 --> 01:27:32,636
All saw increases in revenues too.

805
01:27:32,636 --> 01:27:37,596
And moviegoers in America generated nearly $12 billion for the industry.

806
01:27:37,596 --> 01:27:46,596
There are other reasons to be sceptical of the suggestions that the rising popularity of Netflix is to blame for the perceived decline of cinema.

807
01:27:47,496 --> 01:27:53,996
Comparing the trends in cinema revenues and streaming services tells us little about how one impacts the other.

808
01:27:54,636 --> 01:28:01,336
Just like the consumption of mozzarella cheese can't really explain the rise in the number of civil engineering doctorates awarded.

809
01:28:01,636 --> 01:28:04,136
Even though they're both going up.

